# M3.1 - is the read loop vectorized?
#
# PLAN.md M3.1 Verify: "objdump: the read loop is vectorized (vpaddq on ymm)".
# Command: objdump -d --no-show-raw-insn \
#            build/release/CMakeFiles/bench_core.dir/src/workloads/mem_bw.cpp.o
# g++ 13, -O3 -march=native, Intel Core Ultra 9 185H.
#
# sum_words() is inlined into MemBwWorkload::run_batch(). The read loop is the two
# instructions at 7a4/7a8: two 256-bit accumulators (ymm0, ymm1), 64 bytes folded per
# iteration with vpaddq taking its second operand straight from memory. The eight scalar
# accumulators in the source became two ymm registers, which is what "8 lanes" was for.
# The xmm vpaddq instructions that follow are the horizontal reduction at the end of a
# pass, not the loop. vmovntdq appears in the --nt write and copy paths; vpbroadcastq +
# vmovdqu %ymm0 is the plain write path.
#
# Full disassembly of run_batch() (435 instructions):

